    {
      "page_idx": 21,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The biggest differences between Japan and American have come in slogans and ad copy.Although English is often used .it’s “japanized”english—the sort  that would have  native speakers shaking their head while the japanese nod happily in recognition “let’s spring”was the motto for one of their highly successful ad campaigns."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "日本和美国最大的差异来自于标语和广告语。尽管，它们经常用英语表达，但却是一种“日本式”英语。是那种会让以英语为母语的人摇头难以接受，日本人却点头欣然理解的语言。“let's spring\"就是一个他们大获成功的广告宣传的经典语录。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "image_path": "images/page_21_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 22,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pogue, visiting frequently from his base in California supervised seven resident American Disney managers who work side by side with Japanese counterparts from Oriental Land Co. to keep the park in turn with the Disney doctrine American it may be,but Tokyo Disney land appeals to such deep—seated japanese passions as cleanliness,order,standing service,and technological wizardry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pouge,频繁视察位于加利福利亚的（迪士尼）大本营，指导过七位驻美迪士尼经理的他，与东方乐园株式会社的日本方面负责人携手合作，致力于使此公园逐步贴近“迪士尼主义”，它也许是美国人的，但在日本的迪士尼乐园展现出了日本人在某些方面根深蒂固的热爱，例如整洁，秩序，杰出的服务和魔幻般的工艺。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "image_path": "images/page_22_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 23,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 0,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Japanese executives are impressed by Disney’s detailed training manuals ,which teach employees how to make visitors feel like VIPs.Most worth emulating .say the Japanese ,is Disney’s ability to make even the lowliest job seem glamorous,”they have change the image of dirty work .”said Hakuhodo Institute’s Sekizawa."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "日本高管也被迪士尼的训练手册所震撼，它用来授予员工如何使顾客感受到VIP的待遇。最值得效仿的的地方是，迪士尼有一种使最平凡的工作都看似深富魅力的本领。“他们改变了对苦活的映像”，博报堂的光泽英彦如是说。"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
